1
00:00:06,215 --> 00:00:07,966
[shouts] Hey, are you even listening?

2
00:00:11,303 --> 00:00:12,888
RED LIGHT ELEGY

3
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:17,100
What's with that innocent look
on your face?

4
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:22,231
Sorry to ask this so suddenly,
but can you give me back 3.6 million yen?

5
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:24,399
Instead of those guys.

6
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:26,401
-[♪ tense music playing]
-[Satoshi mumbles]

7
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:28,570
I...

8
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:31,365
[debt collector] I'm counting on you.

9
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,534
Those guys are the only ones who can pay.

10
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:37,621
Hey! Let go of that idiot.
He's just a customer.

11
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:38,705
[tuts]

12
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,959
There's no way, right?

13
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:43,752
And you stink!

14
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:47,047
[Chiko's mom] You're really something.

15
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,299
He's not paying
because he didn't borrow any.

16
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:52,719
Since the husband isn't here,
the wife is obviously going to pay.

17
00:00:52,803 --> 00:00:54,137
Don't you even know that?

18
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:55,514
Maybe I do!

19
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:59,559
He hasn't come back at all, so he must be
wandering around somewhere.

20
00:00:59,643 --> 00:01:04,439
We've got a court order here, you know.
We're gonna have your account seized!

21
00:01:04,523 --> 00:01:07,568
Then take this.
There aren't that many bottles here.

22
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:11,572
[sighs]
In a lousy little factory like this,

23
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:13,949
that attitude of yours won't cut it.

24
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:16,994
Well, that's just your luck then.

25
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:23,208
Hey! If you can make use of that kid,
you can pay me back in one fell swoop.

26
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:27,462
If you master the Zenritsu Zen Massage,
you'll be the best.

27
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:32,301
What an idiot.
I'm busy here so get out already.

28
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:35,012
[debt collector]
You can't act like that towards me.

29
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:39,933
I'm telling you to pay me back
the money he borrowed.

30
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:44,980
Well, then, should I smash
that "luck" of yours to pieces?

31
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,898
I'll marinate it and make gumbo!

32
00:01:46,982 --> 00:01:50,319
You're just a pathetic nobody,
now get out of here!

33
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:53,071
-Why, you little brat!
-Wait a minute.

34
00:01:53,155 --> 00:01:55,824
I'll pay some interest,
so please forgive us!

35
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:58,535
What are you talking about?
You've got no right!

36
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:02,289
Let me handle this! Chiko,
you've always been looking out for me.

37
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:06,918
[exclaims] All right then! Let's do this!

38
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:09,046
So, what do you got?

39
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:11,798
-30,000 yen at the store--
-[gasps]

40
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:17,220
-[Chiko] Are you all right?
-This is a really dangerous thing.

41
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:20,057
-[gagging]
-You'll turn to stone, you piece of crap!

42
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,643
Are you okay?

43
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:25,771
[Chiko's mom]
Did this guy even use his brain?

44
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:28,523
I don't know. He just ran into me.

45
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,318
Anyway, I'll be back.

46
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:36,156
[Chiko] I'm going to call an ambulance.

47
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:38,742
I'm okay.

48
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:42,704
I'm used to pretending to faint.

49
00:02:42,788 --> 00:02:46,208
You're quite the performer, aren't you?

50
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:48,669
I can throw up here, but...

51
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:50,128
I can't make a mess here.

52
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:52,756
[Chiko's mom laughs]

53
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:56,927
I'm back.
Minako always ends up leaving first.

54
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,221
[panting]

55
00:03:00,097 --> 00:03:01,348
Is he your new boyfriend?

56
00:03:03,225 --> 00:03:06,520
-[Chiko] Don't get the wrong idea!
-[yells] Ow!

57
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:09,314
He's not.

58
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:10,982
That really hurt.

59
00:03:11,858 --> 00:03:13,944
[♪ light music playing]

60
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:15,237
[Inaba chuckles]

61
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,656
-[Inaba] Satoshi, you're acting weird.
-Oh, deadass?

62
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,658
-Do you know what that word means?
-[giggles]

63
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,326
Learned it from Chiiko, didn't you?

64
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:23,203
Still saying stuff like that.

65
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:26,498
It's obvious you like Chiko.

66
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:29,626
It's obvious
that it's unrequited love, but...

67
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:32,587
-I'm still curious about it.
-Just leave it at that.

68
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:35,924
Well, that is true,
but I did go to Chiko's house.

69
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:39,845
Huh? I asked her so many times,
but she never told me a thing.

70
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:42,597
No, that's not okay. That's a crime.

71
00:03:42,681 --> 00:03:45,392
Well, well, never mind that.

72
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:47,853
-Huh?
-Did you do it?

73
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:50,147
Don't be quick to say that.

74
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,982
We're not just that relationship.

75
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:53,775
We're soulmates.

76
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:58,321
What's with that foreign word? It's scary.

77
00:03:58,405 --> 00:03:59,489
What do you mean?

78
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:02,993
Aren't you getting dumped?

79
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:06,580
Chiko seems to still be hung up on her ex,

80
00:04:07,289 --> 00:04:09,666
so she'll probably find a new one soon.

81
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:12,502
You need to get her on a date
and make a move on her.

82
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:17,007
If she doesn't want to,
then I won't be disappointed.

83
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,761
Youth is just a fleeting moment.

84
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:32,773
-[rain pattering softly]
-[engine idling]

85
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:41,031
Oh, Chiko.

86
00:04:41,573 --> 00:04:44,075
-Good work today. You're done already?
-Yeah.

87
00:04:46,161 --> 00:04:48,538
If you'd like, drink this later, please.

88
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:52,959
Thanks.

89
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:02,594
Chiko...

90
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,138
This is...

91
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:09,059
-Hey, shouldn't we go now?
-Yeah...

92
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:13,104
Do you think...

93
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,734
Could you switch shifts with me
the day after next?

94
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:18,819
[Chiko] Huh?

95
00:05:18,902 --> 00:05:21,822
-I'm the one who's gonna say that.
-Yeah, you're right.

96
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:24,658
Oh...

97
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,868
Speaking of which,

98
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:29,621
are you free next time?

99
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:31,790
Huh?

100
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,585
[♪ light exciting music playing]

101
00:05:37,254 --> 00:05:38,547
[Chiko] Waited long?

102
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,049
Oh, no, I just got here.

103
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:43,260
Sorry to bother you on your day off.

104
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:45,637
The senior who opened the shop
is annoying.

105
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:49,391
Oh, no, I'm just happy
to hang out with you even on my day off.

106
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,851
Idiot.

107
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:52,811
BIG ZAM

108
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:54,771
[Chiko] He's got a screw loose,

109
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:57,524
-so don't expect much from his cooking.
-[Satoshi] Okay.

110
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:04,197
-[door closes]
-[doorbell jingles]

111
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:09,452
Hey, Chiko! Thanks for coming!

112
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:10,537
Over here!

113
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,705
Excuse me for coming.

114
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,915
-Go ahead and sit right here!
-[patting on chair]

115
00:06:17,711 --> 00:06:19,880
It's been ages, hasn't it?

116
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:22,591
I didn't even come here for lunchtime.

117
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:25,969
[shop owner]
You're full of energy, aren't you?

118
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:31,224
You're not that guy, are you?

119
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:34,561
-Is he within range?
-[Chiko] He's within range.

120
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,313
Doing a part-time job or you lying?

121
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:38,273
No, I'm working on getting my license.

122
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:39,941
[shop owner] Did you get it?

123
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:43,737
You kept saying "Torutoru,"
so isn't that a "Torutoru" scam?

124
00:06:44,404 --> 00:06:47,032
Yusaku should be coming out
any minute now.

125
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,867
That's none of my business.

126
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,785
[shop owner] You two are a perfect match.

127
00:06:51,453 --> 00:06:53,538
Glad things worked out for you.

128
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:57,792
Before Yusaku disappeared, the two of us
used to ride around on a Jiz all the time.

129
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:01,379
That time we got into a fight in Hiroshima
was a classic.

130
00:07:01,463 --> 00:07:04,924
You said you'd thrown 10 guys into a kiln.
[laughs]

131
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:06,760
I'd totally forgotten about that.

132
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,471
-[shop owner] It was pretty wild.
-So?

133
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:12,390
-[Chiko] What kind of place is this?
-Oh, that's right!

134
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:13,933
How shall I put it?

135
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:15,393
In a nutshell,

136
00:07:15,477 --> 00:07:19,314
I'm serving my original dishes
in a dining bar.

137
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:21,816
It was originally supposed to be
a snack bar.

138
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:25,528
I'm making a prototype right now,
so hold on a sec.

139
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,865
[Chiko] A prototype?

140
00:07:29,908 --> 00:07:34,245
Well, here's the new Osaka specialty
I came up with: Okonomi Ramen!

141
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:38,500
-Hironi, there was a finger in it.
-[Hironi] I thought it was just hot.

142
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:39,584
Thanks for the food.

143
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,965
[slurping]

144
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:48,885
[Satoshi choking]

145
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:52,931
[Chiko gags, groans]

146
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:55,642
[angrily] What the heck is this?

147
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:59,729
Since you guys are the 14th and 15th
guys to try it, now I know it sucks.

148
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:02,399
Yeah, I get it now!

149
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,650
What is this?

150
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:07,362
-[Hironi] Come again!
-Thank you.

151
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:11,950
He's charging 2,000 yen for that.

152
00:08:12,701 --> 00:08:13,827
I'll pay.

153
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:16,788
Wait, I'm the one
who got dragged into this.

154
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:18,289
Is it okay?

155
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:21,334
I need a bathroom. I'll be back.

156
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,253
-[door opens]
-Thank you for the meal.

157
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:26,297
-Hey, you're back!
-[Chiko] I need a bathroom.

158
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:30,802
[indistinct chatter]

159
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:35,682
[Ishibashi exclaims]

160
00:08:36,725 --> 00:08:40,895
-Hey! Hey, hey, hey!
-[♪ tense music playing]

161
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:44,566
Gurosuke, what are you doing here?

162
00:08:45,442 --> 00:08:47,736
I called you, but you ignored me,
didn't you?

163
00:08:47,819 --> 00:08:48,903
You mocking me?

164
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:51,781
-Hey! Hey!
-[indistinct chatter]

165
00:08:52,741 --> 00:08:53,992
Stop it!

166
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,202
Just stop already.

167
00:08:56,286 --> 00:08:58,580
-Hey.
-I'm not paying you any more money.

168
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:01,291
Huh? Are you kidding me?

169
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,417
Hey!

170
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,543
-[grunts]
-[thuds]

171
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:05,295
What the heck are you doing?

172
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:08,590
What the heck was that for?

173
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:09,716
Huh?

174
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:13,053
-Ishi-chan?
-What are you looking at?

175
00:09:13,136 --> 00:09:16,431
Hey, why are you fighting
in front of my store?

176
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:22,896
You have your eyes set
on a cute girl, huh?

177
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,773
If you'd like, why not come inside?

178
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:27,650
As an apology,
why not stay and have delicious food?

179
00:09:27,734 --> 00:09:31,154
-[Ishibashi] Let go of me.
-Don't be so rough.

180
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,822
Huh? [breathing nervously]

181
00:09:34,783 --> 00:09:36,534
-[Hironi] All right! Welcome in!
-Pizza?

182
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,828
-[Ishibashi] Pizza?
-[Hironi] Going for pizza?

183
00:09:38,912 --> 00:09:41,623
Looks like someone opened the door.

184
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:44,667
-Are you really okay?
-Yeah.

185
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,713
I'm sorry.

186
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:51,007
That guy's a loser.

187
00:09:52,759 --> 00:09:54,177
[Chiko] See ya!

188
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:09,442
[Chiko]<i> I'll be getting my license soon.</i>

189
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,821
<i>Then I'll work for a delivery company.</i>

190
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:16,574
<i>You'd better do your best.</i>

191
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:28,461
[♪ pensive music playing]

192
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:35,218
[indistinct chatter]

193
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:45,770
Oh? Big Brother.

194
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,064
-Hello.
-Oh.

195
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:49,983
[Satoshi's brother] Hey.

196
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,527
[whispers] Lend me some cash.

197
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:55,738
Sayaka wants to go to karaoke.
I don't have much money.

198
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:57,866
So, you can lend me some, right?

199
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:01,828
I don't have much money right now!

200
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,377
-Let me borrow your bike.
-That's okay with me.

201
00:11:14,716 --> 00:11:16,384
[Satoshi's brother] What's his deal?

202
00:11:19,053 --> 00:11:20,388
[Sayaka] Not sure.

203
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,854
Chiko.

204
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:29,147
Chiko.

205
00:11:30,273 --> 00:11:31,608
Chiko.

206
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:33,776
Chiko.

207
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,404
Chiko!

208
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:39,115
[♪ gentle emotional music playing]

209
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:44,329
[exclaims]

210
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:54,631
[panting]

211
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:27,372
[Chiko] Oh, Satoshi.

212
00:12:27,455 --> 00:12:29,791
Hey. [panting]

213
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:33,419
I wanted to see you.

214
00:12:33,503 --> 00:12:37,215
[Chiko] What are you talking about?
We just saw each other earlier.

215
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,467
[chuckles] Most of the day too.

216
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,760
I'm sorry.

217
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:44,973
But... I want to talk to you.

218
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:46,099
[Chiko] Okay.

219
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:48,101
Hold on.

220
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,355
-[Chiko grunts]
-[rattling]

221
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:09,706
What is it?

222
00:13:18,548 --> 00:13:19,632
I...

223
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,969
like you, Chiko.

224
00:14:25,782 --> 00:14:27,200
[Satoshi] Morning already.

225
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:30,036
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

226
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,710
[Inaba] Oh, Satoshi.

227
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:42,215
Chiko quit.

228
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:43,424
[traffic cone thuds]

229
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:46,969
Didn't you guys work
at a different site yesterday?

230
00:14:47,053 --> 00:14:52,767
[sucks teeth] She asked me
not to tell you until Monday, but...

231
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,269
-did something happen?
-[♪ somber music playing]

232
00:15:01,651 --> 00:15:02,985
Oh, no, no.

233
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:05,988
It's all my fault.

234
00:15:06,697 --> 00:15:09,450
It's not your fault. Did you confess?

235
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:17,500
[Inaba exhales deeply, inhales deeply]

236
00:15:25,383 --> 00:15:27,802
[♪ somber music continues]

237
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:35,601
ROAD STOP

238
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:40,481
[passerby 1] The road is closed.

239
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:42,024
[passerby 2]
Looks like we can't go through.

240
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,863
That's a shame.

241
00:15:52,285 --> 00:15:55,538
[kids] We're back!

242
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:57,456
[adults] Welcome back!

243
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,125
[cook] Okinawa-chan, come for a drink.

244
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,334
[kids] Okay!

245
00:16:00,418 --> 00:16:02,753
-[kid] See you later!
-See you later, guys!

246
00:16:05,131 --> 00:16:08,259
Seriously, what's going on?

247
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:09,552
[Satoshi] Yeah.

248
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:12,471
If I hadn't said anything,
she wouldn't have quit, right?

249
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:15,016
Even if you said something,

250
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:16,809
there's nothing you can do.

251
00:16:16,893 --> 00:16:18,144
The start is what matters.

252
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,979
So let's start from there, okay?

253
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:32,909
This is the first time
I've fallen in love like this. [sniffles]

254
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:36,370
My heart's pounding so hard,
it hurts. [sniffles]

255
00:16:38,456 --> 00:16:41,542
[Inaba] I think Chiko was happy too.

256
00:16:41,626 --> 00:16:44,045
-How do you know that?
-[Inaba] I'm not stupid.

257
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:46,756
No one gets upset
when someone says, "I like you."

258
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,676
And there's no way she'd just disappear
without saying anything.

259
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,261
[customer 1] Ton-chan.

260
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:54,055
[customer 2] Ton-chan, wake up!

261
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:55,431
[customers] Cheers.

262
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:58,267
Satoshi, you've got to get a response.

263
00:16:58,351 --> 00:16:59,518
Huh?

264
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,520
Call Chiko right now.

265
00:17:01,604 --> 00:17:04,023
If you don't, you won't rest easy.

266
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:05,900
Wait, but...

267
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:07,026
Huh?

268
00:17:08,236 --> 00:17:10,488
Hey, why do you know this by heart?

269
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:23,584
Her phone's turned off. [sniffles]

270
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:29,549
Why don't you go visit her house?

271
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:33,135
That's just stalking, isn't it?

272
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:36,472
Is that so?

273
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:48,317
-[Chiko's sister] What do you want?
-[gasps]

274
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:51,654
-Who are you?
-Who am I?

275
00:17:52,655 --> 00:17:54,323
C-Chiko.

276
00:17:54,407 --> 00:17:56,492
Oh, Sis. She hasn't been home in a while.

277
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:58,494
-She hasn't come back?
-Mm.

278
00:17:58,578 --> 00:18:00,538
Sis, she always lived at home.

279
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:02,623
She hasn't been back for two weeks now.

280
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:05,501
[Satoshi] Oh. Is that so?

281
00:18:05,585 --> 00:18:07,795
I wonder where she is.

282
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:11,674
Uh, I don't know.
It depends on her mood where she goes,

283
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,342
so we've given up looking.

284
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:15,636
Is that so?

285
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,222
Thank you.

286
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:19,849
See ya.

287
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:30,776
[Satoshi] Mr. Nagata,
I need to talk to you for a second.

288
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,903
[Inaba] Today's no good.
I'm meeting my daughter.

289
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:35,531
-It's been three years. I want to see her.
-[Satoshi] Huh? Huh?

290
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:37,533
Let's go out for drinks sometime.

291
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:53,257
[vehicle approaching]

292
00:18:53,341 --> 00:18:54,425
[horn honking]

293
00:18:55,885 --> 00:18:58,638
Please wait a moment.
I'm tidying up right now.

294
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:00,973
-[honking continues]
-What?

295
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,519
Chiko?

296
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:09,982
I was getting driving practice,
so I can finally get my license.

297
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:11,817
Isn't it dangerous to drive right after?

298
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:13,611
It is dangerous.

299
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:14,904
You went to see me today.

300
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:17,239
So sorry about that.

301
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:19,659
You apologize without thinking.

302
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:21,577
[Chiko sighs]

303
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:22,995
Hey.

304
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:25,122
-[patting on truck door]
-Drive with me?

305
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:27,792
A drive?

306
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:30,920
[engine rumbling]

307
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:39,053
Chiko, where have you been?

308
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:45,935
I was in Kyoto, Shiga, Fukui, and Gifu

309
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:48,396
for driving practice.

310
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:54,360
Where are we going now?

311
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:57,738
The beach, maybe?

312
00:19:57,822 --> 00:20:00,116
Oh, the beach sounds nice.

313
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:12,294
Why did you blurt that out
all of a sudden?

314
00:20:15,673 --> 00:20:16,799
Well...

315
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,844
I did say it out of the blue,

316
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:22,304
but I've liked you for a long time.

317
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,098
-[Chiko gasps]
-[tires screeching]

318
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:25,558
[Chiko] Again?

319
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,477
-Don't say things like that so suddenly!
-I'm sorry.

320
00:20:28,561 --> 00:20:30,396
[breathing heavily]

321
00:20:36,694 --> 00:20:39,071
[♪ pensive music playing]

322
00:20:39,155 --> 00:20:42,158
[Chiko] <i>How long do you plan</i>
<i>on working as a traffic worker?</i>

323
00:20:43,743 --> 00:20:44,910
[Satoshi] <i>Mm...</i>

324
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:50,666
<i>Even if I quit now, I don't have</i>
<i>anything I want to do like you do.</i>

325
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:56,255
<i>But I don't think</i>
<i>I'll keep doing this forever.</i>

326
00:20:57,173 --> 00:20:59,967
<i>I get yelled at, it gets hot,</i>

327
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:02,803
<i>it doesn't feel good</i>
<i>and I'm scared of cars.</i>

328
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:07,933
<i>But lately, I've been able to see you</i>
<i>and talk to you,</i>

329
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:11,061
<i>and it's been fun.</i>

330
00:21:16,025 --> 00:21:19,904
[waves splashing gently]

331
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:23,157
[Satoshi] Chiko, what's your real name?

332
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:25,409
[Chiko chuckles softly]
Why all of a sudden?

333
00:21:25,493 --> 00:21:26,911
It's Tomoko.

334
00:21:27,495 --> 00:21:30,372
-Use the kanji for "fire under water."
-[Satoshi] Huh?

335
00:21:31,248 --> 00:21:35,002
I also use the same character
for my name, Satoshi.

336
00:21:35,085 --> 00:21:36,545
[Chiko chuckles softly] Really?

337
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:39,131
This is fate.

338
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:40,466
Our character's the same!

339
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:42,718
[chuckles softly]

340
00:21:42,802 --> 00:21:43,886
[chuckles]

341
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,190
As for why I quit,

342
00:21:56,899 --> 00:21:59,819
it's because I get too shy
when I'm with you.

343
00:22:00,903 --> 00:22:01,946
Huh?

344
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:08,369
I was going down an unfamiliar road

345
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,831
when I suddenly saw your face.

346
00:22:15,501 --> 00:22:17,378
I couldn't help but laugh.

347
00:22:23,634 --> 00:22:24,802
Chiko...

348
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:54,665
[♪ gentle music playing]

349
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:57,209
From now on,

350
00:22:58,752 --> 00:23:00,838
I'm talking to you casually.

351
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:04,466
Okay.

352
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:07,761
-Don't just say "okay."
-[chuckles] Sorry.

353
00:23:07,845 --> 00:23:09,722
Don't just say "sorry."

354
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:11,724
-[grunting]
-[water splashes]

355
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,767
[chuckles softly]

356
00:23:16,687 --> 00:23:19,690
From now on, call me Chiko.

357
00:23:21,442 --> 00:23:24,862
[chuckling softly]

358
00:23:30,743 --> 00:23:35,664
Recommended gourmet food in Osaka
Senbayashi specialty: grilled offal.

359
00:23:35,748 --> 00:23:37,833
[indistinct chatter]

360
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:39,001
[seller 1] 200 yen.

361
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:41,128
RAW BEEF

362
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:42,588
[sizzling]

363
00:23:44,173 --> 00:23:46,675
[Satoshi] Oh, it looks good.

364
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:49,887
-[seller 2] Here you go.
-Thank you very much.

365
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:56,477
[Chiko] Mmm!

366
00:23:57,519 --> 00:23:59,104
-That's good.
-[chuckles] Isn't it?

367
00:23:59,772 --> 00:24:00,981
[Satoshi] That's good.

368
00:24:01,065 --> 00:24:02,942
TANAHARA SHOP

369
00:24:03,025 --> 00:24:05,444
[♪ closing theme music playing]

370
00:24:35,557 --> 00:24:37,977
[inaudible]

371
00:25:08,757 --> 00:25:10,759
Translated by Samantha M
